## What I did

**The tree was broken when I started** — the in-flight brand-picker work didn't typecheck (`useBrands` imported but unused, `bind('brandId')` on a narrowed union). Finishing it was the first job.

**1. Cloud Run deploy workflow** (your TODO #1) — `.github/workflows/deploy-cloud-run.yml`, a *second* path alongside the existing GHCR/compose one rather than a replacement. Cloud Run can't pull from GHCR, so it rebuilds the same five Dockerfiles into Artifact Registry. WIF auth (no key in repo settings), migrations as a Cloud Run Job with `--wait` before the API revision exists, `v*` tags only, never from a PR.

The topology difference matters: behind the compose proxy the bundles are same-origin with the API and `CORS_ORIGINS` is correctly empty; on Cloud Run each service is its own origin, so an empty allowlist gives you an API that passes `/health/ready` and refuses every browser call. The preflight job treats it as required.

**2. plan.md items** (TODO #2) — brand picker done (needed a `GET /admin/catalog/brands` route first; the brands table also stopped inferring its list from a page of products, and the products list gained the brand filter its own comment had promised). Filter alignment done — both rows were `align-items: flex-end`, which measures from each child's *last* box; a hinted select had its control lifted a step, and `DayRangeForm` wrapping at 768px dragged both selects down.

**3. Committed** (TODO #3), excluding your `tasks.md` scratch note.

## Verified vs. not

All five gates pass: typecheck, lint, format, test (5330 across 354 suites), build, plus `npm run openapi` regenerating byte-identically.

**The Cloud Run workflow has never run.** No gcloud, no GCP project here. I exercised what I could — YAML job graph, `bash -n` on every block, and the four logic blocks against fixtures with gcloud stubbed. That last one caught a real bug: `[ -n "$X" ] && args+=(…)` **exits under `set -e`** when the test is false, so a deploy without `CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE` would have died silently. It's an `if` now. Untested: whether the service account has the right roles, whether the Secret Manager names exist, whether a revision starts.

The filter fix is **arithmetic, not rendering** — nothing here draws pixels.

## Three things worth your attention

- **`plan.md`'s rewrite broke ~dozens of code comments.** They cite `plan.md K14`, `J1`, `§7`, `§ "Cash on delivery"` and none resolve in the new file. I added a header with the git commits that hold each series (verified all three resolve) rather than restoring the old board.
- **CLAUDE.md said "the repo has no git remote" — that's stale.** `origin` exists and `origin/development` is fetched and level with HEAD. That sentence was the stated reason CI "has never fired", so I downgraded several claims from known-untrue to *unverified from here*. Your Actions tab settles it in a minute.
- **"add page for add more staffs" I did not build**, because it's three different pages and picking wrong is a screen plus its specs. `/admin/operators` already exists but is `PLATFORM_ADMIN`-only, so an ordinary `SELLER_ADMIN` can't invite anyone; the retailer-side `/api/v1/staff` has no operator-facing route at all. I wrote the three options into plan.md — the cheapest real win is probably widening the existing roster, but that's an access decision about accounts that can move money.

Also still open: the remaining filter tab strips (`AdminFilterPills` on leads/replenishment/purchase-orders/trips, plus schemes) — the queue's conversion is the pattern to follow. And "maintain sub nav instead of tabs" appears already satisfied — `AdminSectionNav` is an underline sub-nav, not a tab control — so that one may have meant something I'm not seeing.

