    "summary": "ALTITUDE — the new `.button.button` block re-declares four *properties* (`min-height`, `padding-inline`, `border-radius`, `font-size`) from a file whose own top-of-file doc says it is \"a *token overlay*, not a stylesheet… Because every component in `@udaan/web-ui` … reads `var(--token)` and never a literal, re-declaring a token here re-colours and re-sizes all of them at once.\" `Button.css` is the one component that breaks that premise: it writes `min-height: 44px` as a literal and reads `--text-base`/`--radius-xl`/`--space-9`, which are *scale* tokens shared with body copy and inputs, so there is no token the desk can re-declare to move only the button. The depth-correct fix is to tokenise `Button.css` (a `--control-min-height` / `--control-padding-inline` / `--control-radius` / `--control-font-size` set declared in `tokens.css`), which the overlay then re-states in its `:root` block like every other desk value. Instead the mechanism is bypassed with a doubled selector, and the cost is already visible in this same diff: `AdminShell.css:460` had to be escalated from `.admin-shell__you .button` to `.admin-shell__you .button.button` purely to stay ahead of it, and `.button.button--on-brand` (line 672) now restates all four of `Button.css`'s chip values a second time to stay out of its way.",
    "failure_scenario": "The next `@udaan/web-ui` control the desk needs to resize (TextField, the chip, a future control) has no token to overlay either, so it gets its own doubled property block; each one forces every admin sheet that already styles that control to grow a class, and specificity — not the cascade order the overlay was designed around — becomes the thing holding the desk together. Nothing renders the desk, so the first symptom is a control drawn at the wrong size on a screen nobody opened."
