## TODO 2 — Pending items by priority

**Filters are menus now, not tabs** (the plan's open item). The argument that made this worth doing rather than taste: since the desk was transcribed from `design.html`, filters and `AdminSectionNav` were *the same underline tab strip*, and on three screens one sat directly under the other — one navigating, one filtering, distinguished only by `aria-current` vs `aria-pressed`, which is nothing to a sighted user. Five strips converted; `AdminFilterPills` and `AdminSegmented.css` deleted.

Two things fell out. The spec had pre-declared the trigger for sharing the filter row — *"a third filter row"* — and this made seven, so `DeskFilterBar` is that honoured. And three filters were **actively lying**: purchase orders, trips and leads each offered a hand-written subset of the statuses their own guard accepts, so `?status=RECEIVED` filtered the list while the select displayed "All". All three now derive options and guard from one table.

**Buttons match `design.html`** — 14px/9px radius/16px padding. Notably `desk.css`'s own token comments already *named* those values; the button never read them.

## What I'd flag

Height is the one place I went against both the design and my first draft. I initially took the design's 40px with 44px under `pointer: coarse` — the pattern used twice elsewhere. Review caught that `pointer` reports the *primary* input, so a touchscreen laptop answers `fine`; those precedents each govern one control, whereas this reaches every button including the cash forms. Four pixels against an artboard wasn't worth a class of device losing the touch floor, so the height stays and the desk takes only the look.

Review also caught three defects I'd introduced, each the pattern this repo keeps recording — a rule present, correct, attached to the wrong box. The worst: `:not(.button--on-brand)` is (0,3,0), which outranked the rail's Sign-out rule and would have re-created a two-line "Sign / out" wrap a browser found in September. All three are fixed and now spec-guarded.

**Nothing here has been rendered.** These are arithmetic-over-stylesheets fixes; 390px is where to look first. `CLAUDE.md` and `plan.md` are updated in the same commit, including four deferred items (tokenising the shared `Button`, the `any-pointer` question, network-loaded select options, the tab strip's 1px lap).

