💬 Done. Here's where things landed.

## 1. Cloud Run service-account dev/prod suffix — already done

This shipped in commits `0590a09` and `94568be`, before this session. I verified rather than assumed: a `resolve` job answers `prod`/`dev` and `.github/actions/gcp-auth` puts the suffix on the service account's local part. Two details are better than what the TODO asked for:

- The rule is **containment, not equality** (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). Since the trigger is a `v*` tag, `refs/tags/v1.4.2` never equals `refs/heads/main` — an equality rule would have sent every release to dev while reading fine in the diff.
- The suffix is on the Cloud Run services and Secret Manager entries too, not just the account, which is what makes a single shared project safe.

**One thing is still genuinely open and I can't close it from here:** the default is `main`, and this repo has no `main` (branches are `development` and `master`). So every release currently resolves to dev. The workflow now warns loudly about it, but `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` has to be set in repository settings — no credential in this sandbox can read or write those.

## 2. Top-priority item: retailer touch targets

plan.md ranked this #2 and the only unambiguous *work* item. Done and verified.

I set up the render harness (~20 min, one-off) rather than reasoning over stylesheets, and that decision paid for itself — **the plan said eleven controls; there were thirteen**, and my first pass got three things wrong in the way this repo keeps documenting: *a rule that is present, correct, and attached to the wrong box.*

- The section-link floor went on `.home__section-link`, which is a real class but not either of the two the eight measured links actually wear.
- The search-field floor on the *box* left the input at 42px — the `--light` border eats the content area. It belongs on the input. That's the same defect one layer inside the one I was fixing.
- `CLEAR` and `Remove` were floored on height only, leaving 35 × 44 — missed sideways.

**Verified: target size 0 on both clients** (was 13), and `apps/admin` stayed at 0, which was the check that mattered for the one change inside `@udaan/web-ui`.

I deliberately did **not** touch the 46 contrast findings. Those are plan.md item #1, and CLAUDE.md records twice that the retailer screens *are* the design and that changing its palette isn't a decision to make from inside the code.

## 3. plan.md updated

Re-ranked (touch targets closed, board back to decision-led), the item rewritten with what was measured, and a new item #8 that fell out of the work: four sheets declare the same section-head link byte-for-byte, so one floor had to be written four times.

CLAUDE.md updated in the sections its own rules require — § "The clients", the specs table, § "State of the world" (including the ninth run and corrected test counts).

## Gates

typecheck, lint, format, test (5378/356), build — all pass. The 17 new tests were checked against the pre-fix sheets: 13 of 21 fail there, so they pin the work rather than passing either way.

I haven't committed — say the word and I will.

One caveat worth flagging: every floor rests on `@media (any-pointer: coarse)`, and the only evidence that query behaves is Chromium's emulation agreeing with itself. That's plan.md item #5 and it got sharper with this change, not softer.

